    "result_text": "All 266 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe owner response now includes an `initials` field, computed as the upper-cased first letters of the first and last name, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nI followed the existing `displayName` pattern (another read-only computed field), making two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema. The build regenerates `OwnerDto` with this field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` that computes initials in `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nSince the mapper is shared across all owner responses, the field appears on both the create (POST) response and subsequent GETs \u2014 which is what the new `Cp07Tests.coreInitials` test exercises (creates an owner \"John / Sur\u2026\", then asserts `$.initials` == `J.S.` on GET). The full suite is green (266 passed).",
